# American English: only the lines that differ from English. The rest is English.

store-gh-key-words = You almost certainly don't need one. Without a key, GitHub allows 60 requests an hour from this computer. With one, it allows 5,000. The key only raises that limit. It is used to look at public files and nothing else. It gives Trindle no way into your account, and you check no permissions when you make it. It is stored on this computer, in your keyring, and sent only to GitHub.
